Upstream issue:  https://github.com/apache/superset/issues/41001
Affects:         Apache Superset 6.1.0
Fixed on master: The roles field was removed from DashboardInfo entirely as part
                 of a broader MCP service refactor (merged ~2026-06-24, confirmed
                 by maintainer rusackas in issue #41001 comment). The problematic
                 code path no longer exists on master.
Backport reason: This charm tracks the 6.1.0 release, which still contains the
                 broken serialization paths. This patch carries the equivalent fix
                 forward until the charm upgrades past the refactor.

Root cause:
  In superset/mcp_service/dashboard/schemas.py, two serialization paths build
  the roles field via:

      RoleInfo.model_validate(role, from_attributes=True)

  With from_attributes=True, Pydantic reads role.permissions (a List[PermissionView]
  FAB ORM relationship) and tries to coerce each PermissionView to str, which calls
  PermissionView.__repr__, which lazy-loads PermissionView.permission. By the time
  the MCP ASGI sub-app serializes the response the SQLAlchemy session is gone:

      sqlalchemy.orm.exc.DetachedInstanceError: Instance <PermissionView> is not
      bound to a Session; lazy load operation of attribute 'permission' cannot proceed

  The fix already existed in the same file: serialize_role_object() correctly
  extracts only the safe scalar fields. This patch replaces both model_validate
  call sites with that helper, and sets permissions=None in serialize_role_object()
  to avoid the secondary lazy-load of PermissionView.permission.name.

Verified by: Canonical superset-k8s-operator team (Task 12 investigation, 2026).
             Confirmed independently by Apache Superset maintainer dosubot in
             issue #41001 comment (2026-06-15).

--- a/superset/mcp_service/dashboard/schemas.py
+++ b/superset/mcp_service/dashboard/schemas.py
@@ -142,9 +142,7 @@
     return RoleInfo(
         id=getattr(role, "id", None),
         name=getattr(role, "name", None),
-        permissions=[perm.name for perm in getattr(role, "permissions", [])]
-        if hasattr(role, "permissions")
-        else None,
+        permissions=None,
     )
 
 
@@ -712,7 +710,7 @@
         if dashboard.tags
         else [],
         roles=[
-            RoleInfo.model_validate(role, from_attributes=True)
+            serialize_role_object(role)
             for role in dashboard.roles
         ]
         if dashboard.roles
@@ -794,7 +792,7 @@
         if getattr(dashboard, "tags", None)
         else [],
         roles=[
-            RoleInfo.model_validate(role, from_attributes=True)
+            serialize_role_object(role)
             for role in getattr(dashboard, "roles", [])
         ]
         if getattr(dashboard, "roles", None)
